@* MainLayoutHeader — Auth project variant (identical fixed chrome in NoAuth, minus the gated
   nav item below). Two independent concerns:
   1. Any Header-placed nav item that carries its own authorization requirement (e.g. "Admin
      Dashboard" below) — wrapped exactly like a gated Sider item, just using MudButton instead
      of MudNavLink since MudAppBar is not a MudNavMenu.
   2. The Profile component slot (<MainLayoutProfile /> below) — included UNCONDITIONALLY,
      with no AuthorizeView around it here, whenever the Layout has a modeled Profile Menu
      element at all (regardless of whether Profile currently has any modeled nav items). Any
      Login/Register-vs-Authorized branching for that surface lives entirely inside
      MainLayoutProfile.razor itself (see app-user-menu-auth-sample.razor) — never here.

   The drawer-toggle span/MudIconButton and the bare <ThemeToggle /> are fixed chrome with no
   OnClick/OnToggle EventCallback wiring in the current scaffold — the drawer toggles via the
   navDrawer.toggle() JS interop and the theme toggles internally. Don't reintroduce callbacks
   that an older scaffold generation used here. *@

<MudAppBar>
    <span onclick="navDrawer.toggle()">
        <MudIconButton Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Menu"
                       Color="Color.Inherit"
                       Edge="Edge.Start" />
    </span>
    <MudButton Href="/" Class="my-2 mr-2" Color="Color.Inherit">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.h5">MyApp</MudText>
    </MudButton>

    <AuthorizeView Roles="Admin">
        <Authorized>
            <MudButton Href="/admin-dashboard" Color="Color.Inherit">Admin Dashboard</MudButton>
        </Authorized>
    </AuthorizeView>

    <MudSpacer />
    <ThemeToggle />
    <MainLayoutProfile />
</MudAppBar>
